{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"The disputes about what an agreement meant are consistent with the agreements having fixed who but not what, when, or to what standard; a written record with concrete task definitions and deadlines would shrink the space of those disputes whether or not any later reinterpretation is bad faith.","scope":"Based only on what the task states; the actual form this flat's agreements take is unobserved.","grounds":"The task reports that flatmates agree on who will do something and later disagree about what the agreement meant."},{"id":"r2","type":"commitment","text":"Confirm every new chore agreement in writing at the moment it is made — task, concrete standard, deadline — in a place all three can see.","action":"After any chore conversation, the asker posts a short confirmation the others can correct on the spot.","consequence":"Later meaning-disputes become disputes about a shared text rather than about memories, and nobody has to be accused of anything.","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r3","type":"problem","text":"The material does not say why the third flatmate has started avoiding the chore conversations; feeling criticized or ganged up on, being outvoted two-to-one, disengagement from the flat, and causes unrelated to chores are all open, and they call for different responses."},{"id":"r4","type":"commitment","text":"Ask the avoidant friend one-on-one, without accusation, what makes the chore conversations hard, before designing or proposing any system on their behalf.","consequence":"The eventual system is designed with that friend rather than for them, and fits the actual cause rather than a guessed one.","depends":["r3"]},{"id":"r5","type":"claim","text":"With changing work schedules, static long-term chore assignments become stale or unfair; short-horizon (weekly) planning plus an explicit swap rule — if your schedule changes, say so and propose a swap rather than letting the task lapse — fits the instability better than a fixed rota.","grounds":"The task states that the flatmates' work schedules change."},{"id":"r6","type":"commitment","text":"Adopt an explicit swap rule: a schedule change triggers a proposed swap in the shared note, never a silent lapse.","depends":["r5"],"mentions":["r2"]},{"id":"r7","type":"claim","text":"Conjecture: if chore conversations are convened mainly when something has gone wrong, then initiating one functions as a complaint signal, and the friend's avoidance may be avoidance of being complained at rather than of chores or of the asker.","scope":"Untested; the trigger pattern of the conversations is not reported.","grounds":"The task reports one friend has started avoiding the conversations; 'started' suggests a change in the situation rather than a fixed trait."},{"id":"r8","type":"commitment","text":"Replace ad-hoc chore talks with a short, scheduled weekly check-in covering assignments against actual schedules, swaps, and schedule changes — mostly forward-looking rather than retrospective.","consequence":"Conversation about chores stops being synonymous with complaint, which may lower its cost for the avoidant friend if r7 holds.","depends":["r5","r7"]},{"id":"r9","type":"objection","text":"An over-engineered chore apparatus among friends can itself become the grievance; visible enforcement reads as policing, and the friendship is a larger asset than any cleaning rota.","bearing":"Any proposed system should be minimal, jointly designed by all three, and cheap to abandon if it costs more goodwill than it saves; the objection cuts against heavy versions of r2, r6 and r8, not against the light versions proposed there.","target":["r2","r6","r8"]},{"id":"r10","type":"claim","text":"Conjecture: chore arguments often involve a perception asymmetry — each person observes their own contributions and few of the others' — so a shared visible record partially corrects each flatmate's evidence about who does what.","scope":"Untested; the content of this flat's arguments is not reported, so it is unknown whether any of them concern who does more."},{"id":"r11","type":"commitment","text":"Hold structural exits open as legitimate endpoints rather than as failures — splitting a cleaner three ways, shrinking the shared surface, or renegotiating the living arrangement — to be weighed only after a fair, minimal, jointly adopted system has been tried in good faith and the friction persists.","consequence":"Prevents system failure from being treated as personal failure and keeps endless argument from being the only imaginable endpoint.","target":["r8"]},{"id":"r12","type":"use","text":"Sequence the uptake: begin with r2 (unilateral written confirmations) and r4 (the direct one-on-one question); move to r8 (the joint weekly check-in) only once r4's answer arrives, so the system is built with the avoidant friend rather than around them.","target":["r2","r4","r8"],"depends":["r9"]}],"uptake":["r2","r4","r6","r8","r12"]}